    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1805">

                <pb facs="1461" n="1345" xml:id="pg1345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/7B.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The conditions at Constantinople described in your telegram of October 31 are
                    naturally creating anxiety here. It is assumed that you would, if occasion
                    arise, find it possible to arrange for extension by the naval forces of the
                    friendly neutral Powers of adequate protection of such American citizens as can
                    not be accommodated on the [station ship] <hi rendition="#italic">Scorpion</hi>.
                    There is no available American vessel nearer than our own shores.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
